1
00:00:00,040 --> 00:00:03,080
Then, on one, unremarkable rock orbiting

2
00:00:03,080 --> 00:00:06,840
one unremarkable star, in one unremarkable

3
00:00:06,840 --> 00:00:09,620
galaxy, the one you named Dirt,

4
00:00:09,660 --> 00:00:10,820
carbon atoms started

5
00:00:10,820 --> 00:00:13,080
doing something unusual.

6
00:00:13,120 --> 00:00:15,000
Carbon is the most promiscuous

7
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:16,980
element in the periodic table.

8
00:00:16,980 --> 00:00:19,580
It will bond with almost anything.

9
00:00:19,700 --> 00:00:21,320
On your particular rock, it

10
00:00:21,320 --> 00:00:23,700
bonded with hydrogen, oxygen, and

11
00:00:23,700 --> 00:00:25,880
nitrogen in arrangements that could

12
00:00:25,880 --> 00:00:29,120
do one very specific trick.

13
00:00:29,180 --> 00:00:30,600
Copy themselves.

14
00:00:31,160 --> 00:00:32,240
This was the moment

15
00:00:32,240 --> 00:00:34,640
everything went wrong.

16
00:00:34,760 --> 00:00:36,180
The molecules that were better

17
00:00:36,180 --> 00:00:38,380
at copying made more copies.

18
00:00:38,380 --> 00:00:39,400
The ones that were worse

19
00:00:39,400 --> 00:00:41,520
at copying made fewer.

20
00:00:41,520 --> 00:00:43,280
This is the entire plot of

21
00:00:43,280 --> 00:00:45,420
the next four billion years.

22
00:00:45,420 --> 00:00:47,160
It is also the entire plot of

23
00:00:47,160 --> 00:00:50,620
your economy, your politics, your wars, and

24
00:00:50,620 --> 00:00:53,620
your inability to fund clinical trials.

25
00:00:53,620 --> 00:00:55,880
Everything else is a footnote.

26
00:00:55,880 --> 00:00:57,980
Including you.

27
00:01:01,160 --> 00:01:01,200
You
